<title>GREECE: Poseidon,Citifund lead Greek fixed-income funds.</title>
<headline>Poseidon,Citifund lead Greek fixed-income funds.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poseidon and Citifund Premium were leading Greece's 40 fixed-income funds in the first half of 1997 with year-to-date returns of 17.83 and 12.53 percent, respectively, the association of institutional investors said.</p>
<p>Fixed-income funds under management reached 1.994 trillion drachmas in end-June, up 45.96 percent since the beginning of the year and 3.37 percent on May.</p>
<p>They made up 37.8 percent of the mutual fund industry's total assets which rose to 5.41 trillion drachmas in the first half of 1997, an increase of 41.84 percent.</p>
